# QEMU Linux-desktop harness artifacts (initramfs, serial log, screendumps)
# ⛔⛔ THE WHOLE BUILD DIRECTORY. It previously ignored only `build/qemu-linux/`, and 29 artifacts were
# tracked — 15 static binaries at ~15 MB each, about 220 MB, plus 62 MB of QEMU screendumps and guest
# images that a run with `AE_QEMU_OUT=build/qemu-a128` slipped past the one named path.
# ⚠ NOTHING REQUIRED THEM COMMITTED. Every reference either BUILDS the artifact
# (`cyrius build --agnos src/main.cyr build/aethersafha-agnos` in the README, CLAUDE.md, the guides) or
# is a `# Run:` header in programs/*.cyr. The one script that READS one —
# `docs/development/agnos-render/aethersafha-smoke.sh:37` — already errors with the exact build command
# when it is absent, which is the correct behaviour and better than finding a stale one.
# ⛔ AND A COMMITTED BUILD ARTIFACT IS ACTIVELY DANGEROUS, not merely large. In the sibling agnos repo
# `tests/gpu/build/edgeasm` was committed, ran, and printed "B4 PASS -- the tool reproduces a shipped
# iron-proven shader byte-for-byte" while `edgeasm.cyr` beside it COULD NOT COMPILE AT ALL. A committed
# binary is evidence about whatever source existed when someone last ran a compiler, not about the
# source next to it.
build/
